                  "from": 246.24501,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2810988,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "One person stayed with each elephant while they waited for the vets to do checks. It was very important to keep an eye on their breathing. If there were fewer than six breaths per minute, the elephant would need urgent medical attention. Collars were fitted to the matriarch in each group so their movements could be tracked in their new home. Measurements were taken of each elephant's tusks.",
            "children": [
